From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: A733 combo-PHY -- lane comments follow the corrected reference

[Recipe cut: regenerated against the instrumentation-free driver; comment changes
only, as before.]

Comment-only. Brings four comments in line with the corrected COMB0 lane reading of
2026-09-17. Those facts were
re-derived twice, independently, from the UM, the pinout
(A733_PINOUT_V0.91), schematic v1.10 p6/p12 and silicon captures:

  - COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL: the UM field is one per PHY lane, selecting
    the DP lane that PHY lane carries, not "one per
    DP lane, physical -> logical".
  - PMA 0xF000 + n * 0x100 bit8: the UM does not define it; "lane invert"
    is the vendor's name. The board swaps P/N on every lane, and the vendor
    sets the bit on all four lanes in USB3 mode too, while our USB3 path
    leaves it clear and links at 10 Gbps.
  - The saved-lane-values comment adds that the vendor stack writes map and
    inverts in USB3 mode, which this driver does not need.
  - The DP entry comment attributed the missing clock recovery to the missing
    inverts. That run had the lane map at its 0xFFFF reset as well, so the
    measurement cannot separate the two.

Not changed, because only one of the two derivations raised it: "COMB0 carries
SuperSpeed or DP, never both", checked against the A733 user manual.

No functional change; the object code is identical apart from line
information.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
@@ -54,8 +54,9 @@
  */
 #define  DP_RAWS_TXDW_CONV_4LANE	(DP_PHY_CFG_DATA_EN | DP_PHY_CFG_LN_EN | \
 					 DP_PHY_CFG_LN_RSTN)
-/* COMB0_PHY_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL (0x06C06C24) -- four 4-bit fields, one per DP
- * lane, physical -> logical. Reset default 0xFFFF; this board's
+/* COMB0_PHY_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL (0x06C06C24) -- four 4-bit fields, one per PHY
+ * lane (LN0 = [3:0]), each selecting which DP lane's raw TX data that PHY lane
+ * carries (A733 user manual). Reset default 0xFFFF; this board's
  * lane_remap = <0 1 2 3> is the identity 0x00003210.
  */
 #define COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL		0x0C24
@@ -124,8 +125,12 @@
 #define  PMA_NUDGE_CLR			(0xF << 8)
 
 /*
- * Per-lane DP config word in the PMA; bit8 inverts the lane. Vendor
- * combo0_dp_lane_invert() walks word index 0xF000 + n * 0x100. NOTE this is
+ * Per-lane config word in the PMA, index 0xF000 + n * 0x100. The vendor names
+ * bit8 a lane invert (combo0_dp_lane_invert()); the UM does not define it, and
+ * no single-variable measurement of it exists. The board swaps P/N on all four
+ * COMB0 lanes (ball COMB0-TXnP -> net LANEn-N in the schematic); the
+ * vendor stack sets bit8 on all four in USB3 mode as well as in DP, while the
+ * USB3 path here leaves it clear and links at 10 Gbps. NOTE this is
  * a BYTE offset, like PMA_NUDGE_OFF above and unlike PMA_DP_LANE_CFG below,
  * which is a raw word index shifted at its call site -- the file carries both
  * conventions, so the names say which.
@@ -253,7 +258,9 @@ struct a733_combophy {
 	/* The DP lane map and lane inverts, and the USB values they displace.
 	 * Written when the mux hands the lanes to DisplayPort and put back when
 	 * it takes them away, so a port that never enters DP alt mode never
-	 * sees either register.
+	 * sees either register from this driver. (The vendor stack writes both
+	 * in USB3 mode too: map 0x3210, bit8 on all four lanes. The USB3 path
+	 * here does not, and needs neither to link at 10 Gbps.)
 	 */
 	u32			dp_lane_map;
 	u32			dp_lane_invert;
@@ -1831,8 +1838,10 @@ static void a733_combophy_dp_lanes_leave(struct a733_combophy *cp)
  * trade this tree does not make.
  *
  * The DP lane map at 0x06C06C24 and the four PMA lane inverts are written from
- * here. Measured consequence of missing inverts: the sink escalates the
- * voltage swing 1 -> 2 -> 3 and never reaches clock recovery.
+ * here. Measured consequence of the missing map and inverts together: the
+ * sink escalates the voltage swing 1 -> 2 -> 3 and never reaches clock
+ * recovery. Both were missing in that run, so it does not say which of the
+ * two was needed.
  *
  * Still missing for actual video, named rather than implied: the DP AUX/HPD
  * front end at 0x06C01E00 (0x03331131 in the capture, 0x00330000 at reset),
